---
/**
 * /en/privacy-policy/ — English version of /politica-de-privacidad/.
 * The rest of /en/ still lives only as a build on the server (no source yet);
 * this page is the first English page with source in the repo.
 * Keep both versions in sync. In case of discrepancy, the Spanish version prevails.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE, URL_POLITICA_DATOS } from '../../config';

const EFFECTIVE = 'November 11, 2026';
const ADDRESS = 'Calle 85 # 50-37, Torre Médica del Mar, Clínica Iberoamérica, office 311, Barranquilla, Atlántico, Colombia';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy · Dr. Elika Luque"
  description="How Dr. Elika Luque collects, uses, protects and processes the personal data of patients and users of draelikaluque.com, in accordance with Colombian Law 1581 of 2012."
  variant="legal"
  lang="en"
  alterna={URL_POLITICA_DATOS}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Data protection · Colombian Law 1581 of 2012"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    sub={`Effective ${EFFECTIVE}. It applies to the data we receive on this website, through our forms, Facebook and Instagram lead ads, WhatsApp, email and at the office.`}
    ctaText=""
  />

  <section class="bg-marfil">
    <div class="wrap py-14 md:py-20">
      <article class="legal">
        <p>
          <a href={URL_POLITICA_DATOS} lang="es" hreflang="es">Leer esta política en español</a>.
          In case of any discrepancy, the Spanish version prevails.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
        <div class="legal-ficha">
          <p><strong>Dr. Elika Luque</strong>, bariatric and laparoscopic surgeon.</p>
          <p><strong>Address:</strong> {ADDRESS}.</p>
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
          <p><strong>Phone and WhatsApp:</strong> {SITE.phone}</p>
          <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href={SITE.url}>draelikaluque.com</a></p>
        </div>
        <p>
          In this policy, "we" means Dr. Elika Luque and her care team (advisors and
          administrative staff). "You" or "the data subject" is the person the data belongs to.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Legal framework</h2>
        <p>
          This policy complies with Colombian Statutory Law 1581 of 2012, Decree 1377 of 2013
          (compiled in Decree 1074 of 2015) and the rules on medical records and medical
          confidentiality (Law 23 of 1981 and Resolution 1995 of 1999). The supervisory
          authority is the Superintendence of Industry and Commerce (SIC).
        </p>

        <h2>3. Data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identification and contact data:</strong> name, WhatsApp or phone number, email, country and city.</li>
          <li><strong>Data about your inquiry:</strong> reason for contact and procedure of interest (for example gastric balloon, sleeve, bypass or reflux).</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Health data (sensitive data):</strong> what you choose to share in the quiz
            or in the assessment, such as weight, height, body mass index (BMI), related
            conditions (high blood pressure, diabetes, apnea, joint pain), reflux, previous
            surgeries or procedures and previous weight-loss attempts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Browsing and campaign data:</strong> the page you contact us from, the
            source of your visit (UTM parameters and Google and Meta click identifiers),
            IP address, browser type and the information collected by the cookies and
            measurement tools described in section 9.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not request data from minors through this website. If a minor needs care,
          their data is provided by their legal representative.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Sensitive data</h2>
        <p>Health data is sensitive data. Therefore:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>You are <strong>not required</strong> to provide it or to answer questions about your health.</li>
          <li>We only process it with your <strong>prior, express and informed consent</strong>, which you give by checking the consent box in our forms or by another verifiable means.</li>
          <li>We use it only to guide you, prepare your assessment and provide medical care.</li>
          <li>No service, appointment or care depends on you providing sensitive data that is not necessary for your care.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Why we use your data (purposes)</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Answer your inquiries and contact you by WhatsApp, phone or email about the service you requested.</li>
          <li>Schedule, confirm and remind you of your pre-assessment, assessment, tests and follow-ups.</li>
          <li>Give you initial guidance (for example, the quiz result) and prepare your medical assessment.</li>
          <li>Provide medical care and follow up on your treatment.</li>
          <li>Send you information about procedures, prices, payment options and care, when you have requested it.</li>
          <li>Send you educational content, news and promotions about our services. You can ask us to stop at any time.</li>
          <li>Measure and improve our website and advertising campaigns, and show relevant ads on platforms such as Google, Facebook and Instagram.</li>
          <li>Comply with legal, accounting and medical-record obligations and respond to requests from authorities.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Medical records are also governed by their own confidentiality and retention rules.</p>

        <h2>6. How we obtain your consent</h2>
        <p>
          Before submitting any of our forms you must check the box authorizing the processing
          of your data under this policy. You may also authorize it in writing, by WhatsApp,
          by email or at the office. If you write to us directly by WhatsApp or email, we
          understand you authorize us to use that data to reply (purposes 1 and 2). We keep
          proof of your consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you leave your data in a Facebook or Instagram lead form, Meta delivers it to
          us so we can contact you, and we process it under this policy.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Who we share your data with</h2>
        <p>We do not sell or rent your personal data. We only share it with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dr. Elika Luque's care team</strong>, bound by confidentiality.</li>
          <li><strong>Clinics and healthcare providers</strong> where your care or tests take place (for example, Clínica Portoazul), when necessary to provide the service.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Providers that process data on our behalf</strong> (processors), only for
            the purposes of this policy: website and database hosting (Google Cloud), email
            (Google Workspace), online scheduling (Calendly), messaging (WhatsApp), measurement
            and advertising (Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, Google Ads and Meta) and the
            marketing agency that manages our campaigns.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, when required by law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Some of these providers store data on servers outside Colombia, mainly in the United
          States. By accepting this policy you authorize that transfer. We only work with
          providers that offer adequate levels of data protection.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Cookies and measurement tools</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses cookies and similar technologies from Google Tag Manager, Google
          Analytics, Google Ads and Meta (Facebook pixel) to understand how the site is used,
          measure our campaigns and show ads to people interested in our services. We also
          store the source of your visit (UTM) in your browser. You can block or delete
          cookies in your browser settings; some site features may not work the same way.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
        <p>As the data subject you have the right to:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Know, update and correct your data.</li>
          <li>Request proof of the consent you gave us.</li>
          <li>Be informed, upon request, of how your data has been used.</li>
          <li>Revoke your consent and request deletion of your data, when there is no legal or contractual duty to keep it (for example, medical records).</li>
          <li>File complaints with the Superintendence of Industry and Commerce, after submitting your inquiry or claim to us.</li>
          <li>Access your personal data free of charge.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>11. How to exercise your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or WhatsApp
          {' '}{SITE.phone}, including your name, ID number, contact details, your request
          and, if applicable, supporting documents. If you act on behalf of someone else,
          attach proof of authorization.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Inquiries</strong> (what data we hold and how we use it): answered within 10 business days, extendable by up to 5 more business days with notice.</li>
          <li><strong>Claims</strong> (correction, update, deletion or revocation): answered within 15 business days, extendable by up to 8 more business days with notice. If a claim is incomplete, we will ask you to complete it within 5 business days; after 2 months without a reply, it is considered withdrawn.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>12. Security and retention</h2>
        <p>
          We protect your data with reasonable technical, human and administrative measures:
          encrypted connection (HTTPS), password-protected access for authorized staff only,
          and providers with recognized security standards. We keep your data as long as
          needed for the purposes of this policy or as required by law. Medical records are
          kept for the period set by law.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy. Significant changes will be published on this page with
          the new effective date. If the purposes change, we will ask for your consent again.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Effective date</h2>
        <p>
          This policy is effective as of {EFFECTIVE}. Data will be processed for as long as
          necessary to fulfill its purposes.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
